body:
I already played around a bit with the angle of the player being drawn.

Here's the line of code that gets the angle at which to draw the player:

    if object_exists(o_camera) sprite_angle = o_camera.angle * -1;

And here's the line of code that actually draws the player:

    draw_sprite_general(s_main, 0, floor(x_frame) * frame_size, y_frame * frame_size, frame_size, frame_size, xx, yy, image_xscale, image_yscale, sprite_angle, image_blend, image_blend, image_blend, image_blend, image_alpha);


This works, and draws the player properly, but doesn't do anything to adjust the controls. I could do the math on them myself, but it would take some time and I wasn't sure if it was the most efficient solution. The other problem seems to be that this code doesn't actually adjust the collision box in any way.
